{
  "summary": "Sabrina Carpenter released “Espresso” on April 11, 2024, as the lead single from *Short n’ Sweet*. Written by Carpenter, Amy Allen, Steph Jones, and producer Julian Bunetta, the song blends pop, funk, and dance influences. Its lyrics celebrate self-confidence and femininity; the playful, grammatically unconventional refrain “That’s that me espresso” also became a meme.\n\nCritics praised the song’s catchy hook, clever lyrics, and infectious groove. It became Carpenter’s first U.S. top-five hit, peaking at number three on the Billboard Hot 100, and topped the Billboard Global 200. It also reached number one in more than 20 countries, including the UK and Australia, and has surpassed 3.2 billion Spotify streams.\n\nA Dave Meyers-directed music video, set around a beach and featuring a comic run-in with the police, accompanied the release. Carpenter performed the song at Coachella, on *Saturday Night Live*, at the MTV Video Music Awards and Grammys, and on her *Short n’ Sweet Tour*. “Espresso” won the 2024 VMA for Song of the Year and earned three Grammy nominations, winning Best Pop Solo Performance and Best Remixed Recording. The song has also appeared in games, television, and commercial collaborations.",
